\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Energy after the other vertices are eliminated}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{\ref{fdip-00DB} computes the resistance between two vertices
of a unit cycle. The reciprocal of that resistance is the
energy of a function whose values at the two vertices differ
by #{1}, after every other vertex has been eliminated. Paths
meeting only at those two vertices add their energies. What
energy does a path of unit edges retain, and what energy does
the cycle retain?}
